<p>EDIT 1: Added details to overall idea. Thanks to @REDESERT (i don't know how to tag lol)</p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A collection of objects with anomalous, antidepressive effects. These objects are (but not limited to): manifestation of feelings described as &quot;relaxation, peacefulness, etc.&quot;, diminished symptoms in subjects diagnosed with major depressive dissorder, etc. Objects interact with each other and are essential between themselves (For example: Access to XXXX-2 can only be done by interacting with XXXX-1, XXXX-3 is stored inside of XXXX-2 and any sample taken will disappear when<br />
exiting XXXX-2)</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Discovered in a lab of an unknown GoI. Consists of an air freshener, a room that can only be accessed by smelling the content of the air freshener, and a lavender plant contained inside the room. The objects manifest anomalous anti-depressive and anti-memetic properties, since subjects exposed to any of the XXXX objects will manifest a general feeling of well-being; but they won't remember any initial exposition. Audiovisual data stored in a digital medium will experience total corruption and will be intelligible, however, textual and analogue data storage doesn't seem to be affected.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> There's a fourth object which is only known to high clearance ranks. It's a virus that is presumably the cause of major depressive disorder and it's linked to the human subconscious since unknown times. Cannot be cured with any current means and it's symptoms can only be diminished with antidepressants. Also, one of the three initial objects has a very high value to the Foundation; it's a Thaumiel, and has a very high possibility to counterattack XXXX-4. Linked to SCP-5000 narrative (or at least I tried)</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I've started writing this SCP, but I would like to know if this idea hasn't been implemented. Also, I'm not a native english speaker, so sorri for may bed england.<br />
<a href="http://scp-sandbox-3.wikidot.com/primedstasis">I've started with a draft in the sandbox</a>, just to familiarise myself with the formatting, and also experimenting a little bit. Helps me to get my ideas clearer too.</p>

